            <ArticleTitle>Radiologic manifestation of the malignant peripheral nerve sheet tumor involving the brachial plexus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>615-619</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.radcr.2017.02.006</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 63-year-old African American female with history of bilateral breast cancer status after lumpectomy and radiation therapy presented with right hand, wrist, and arm pain. She was found to have a right axillary mass and a large lesion in the right brachial plexus. A biopsy of the brachial plexus mass came back as a malignant peripheral nerve sheath tumor. This case report illustrates the critical value of multiple imaging modalities in definitive diagnosis of this rare pathologic entity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
